I walk to the pharmacy in the clinic.
There is a pharmacist at the counter.
I give him the doctor's prescription.
He looks at that prescription.
Then he takes out some tablets and a cough syrup.
"These are the medicines," he says.
"When should I take these tablets?" I ask.
"You must take them morning, afternoon, and night after eating food," he says.
"And the syrup?" I ask.
"You must drink the syrup three times a day," he replies.
I nod in agreement.
"How many rupees is this?" I ask.
"Three hundred and twenty rupees," he says.
I take the money and give it to him.
I put the medicines in my bag.
It is still raining outside.
I take my umbrella and walk home.
